# Your Mother Should Know, verse (figure 126.1)
# Eleven measures, 4 + 3 + 4. The bassline works down the scale under the first phrase, putting
# the A chord of bar 3 in second inversion (E in the bass); Pollack types it only for that phrase.
# Pivot: d is iv in a = ii in C.
#? Pollack's numerals for bars 6 and 9 read "V" under C and "I" under G; with G as V and C as I
#? (as in his fig. 126.3, the same D G C progression) they look like slips. Shown here as G{V} and
#? C{I}; check against the typed view.
key a

